{
 "format": "rustsheet-case/v1",
 "description": "T-4574: DATEDIF, YEARFRAC and DAYS360 with a date argument s just below midnight of N around Excel's fictitious 1900-02-29 (serial 60); 1s = 1/86400. Rows 1-3 N=59, rows 4-6 N=60, rows 7-9 N=61; within each group s = N-0.4s, N-(2^-22+2^-33), N (the integer control). Rows 10-18 the same Ns (10-12 59, 13-15 60, 16-18 61) with s = N-0.6s, fl(N-0.5s) minus one ulp (2^-47 for N in [32,64)), fl(N-0.5s): the half-second cut. A:F DATEDIF(s,425,u) and G:L DATEDIF(31,s,u) for u = d, m, y, md, ym, yd (425 is 1901-02-28, 31 is 1900-01-31). M:Q YEARFRAC(s,425,b) and R:V YEARFRAC(31,s,b) for basis 0-4. W, X DAYS360(s,425,FALSE/TRUE); Y, Z DAYS360(31,s,FALSE/TRUE).",
 "tags": [
  "M6",
  "probe",
  "dates"
 ],
